_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "A genuine time-respecting cascade links 1357 to 1439: 1357->1376 (54609), 1376->818 (54823), 818->786 (55135), 786->1539 (55477), 1539->1439 (55814). Timestamps increase monotonically and all inter-hop gaps (214, 312, 342, 337) are within the 600-unit limit. Each hop was verified individually at its exact timestamp with correct forward direction. Alternative explanations were tested and rejected: static connectivity is uninformative because 1357 sits in a dense hub-rich component; endpoint popularity does not explain the path since the relays (1376, 818, 786, 1539) have only 4-9 events each; and reachability is not degenerate, since the reverse direction 1439->1357 fails entirely and tightening max_wait to 200 also fails, showing the result depends on the actual event timing. Confidence is high but not absolute because exactly one such path exists, making the cascade dependent on a single fragile chain."}, "raw_final_response": "The evidence is clear. Let me summarize:\n\n**Findings:**\n\n1. **A valid time-respecting cascade exists** (step_01, step_03): `1357 \u2192(54609) 1376 \u2192(54823) 818 \u2192(55135) 786 \u2192(55477) 1539 \u2192(55814) 1439`. Timestamps are strictly increasing, and all four inter-hop waits (214, 312, 342, 337) fall under the 600-unit limit \u2014 max used was 342.\n\n2. **Every hop verified independently** (steps 04, 05, 08, 09, 10): each edge exists at its exact claimed timestamp and in the correct forward direction (u\u2192v, zero reverse events). The chain is not an artifact of direction-agnostic matching.\n\n3. **Confounder \u2014 static connectivity is not the explanation** (step_12): 1357 sits in a large, densely connected 2-hop component containing hubs like 62, 81, 302 with dozens of partners. Ignoring time, \"connection\" is nearly guaranteed here, so the static neighborhood alone would be uninformative. The cascade claim rests on the ordered timestamps, not this.\n\n4. **Confounder \u2014 not a trivial/degenerate reachability regime** (step_06, step_11): the reverse direction 1439\u21921357 reaches only 3 nodes and *fails*, showing the temporal ordering genuinely constrains flow rather than everything reaching everything. Tightening max_wait to 200 also **fails** despite reaching 73 nodes \u2014 the path specifically requires the 600-unit budget, meaning the result is a real property of the timing, not saturation.\n\n5. **Confounder \u2014 endpoint popularity is not driving it** (step_07): although 1357 (69 events) and 1439 (68 events) are high-degree, the actual relay nodes 1376, 818, 786, 1539 have only 4\u20139 events each. The cascade runs through low-activity intermediaries, so it cannot be dismissed as noise from busy hubs. Only one such path exists (step_03) \u2014 it is a narrow, specific channel.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_3c29ca6f\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1357, 1376, 818, 786, 1539, 1439],\n  \"window\": [36012, 74411],\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A genuine time-respecting cascade links 1357 to 1439: 1357->1376 (54609), 1376->818 (54823), 818->786 (55135), 786->1539 (55477), 1539->1439 (55814). Timestamps increase monotonically and all inter-hop gaps (214, 312, 342, 337) are within the 600-unit limit. Each hop was verified individually at its exact timestamp with correct forward direction. Alternative explanations were tested and rejected: static connectivity is uninformative because 1357 sits in a dense hub-rich component; endpoint popularity does not explain the path since the relays (1376, 818, 786, 1539) have only 4-9 events each; and reachability is not degenerate, since the reverse direction 1439->1357 fails entirely and tightening max_wait to 200 also fails, showing the result depends on the actual event timing. Confidence is high but not absolute because exactly one such path exists, making the cascade dependent on a single fragile chain.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 35345, "total_output_tokens": 3659, "total_tokens": 39004, "total_latency_ms": 52661, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}